Question: Point $P$ is selected at random from the interior of the pentagon with vertices $A=(0,2)$, $B= (4,0)$, $C = (2\pi +1, 0)$, $D=(2\pi
+1,4)$, and $E=(0,4)$. What is the probability that $\angle APB$ is obtuse? Express your answer as a common fraction.

[asy]
pair A,B,C,D,I;
A=(0,2);
B=(4,0);
C=(7.3,0);
D=(7.3,4);
I=(0,4);
draw(A--B--C--D--I--cycle);
label("$A$",A,W);
label("$B$",B,S);
label("$C$",C,E);
label("$D$",D,E);
label("$E$",I,W);
[/asy]

